course: dictionary
lesson: 10610
title: Uneasily: worried or not settled
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Uneasily tells you how someone feels or how things sit together. It means in a worried, nervous or uncomfortable way. Look for clues in the sentence, such as what a character does or what is happening around them.
explain: In stories, a character who looks around uneasily or shifts uneasily in a chair feels that something is wrong. The author uses this word to warn you that trouble or tension may be coming.
explain: Uneasily can also mean not settled. «Sit uneasily with» means two things do not fit well together. Think of a happy ending that sits uneasily with some sad news: the two do not match.
fact: Uneasily means in a worried, nervous or uncomfortable way.
fact: In stories, «looking around uneasily» shows a character sensing that something is wrong.
fact: «Sit uneasily with» means that two things do not fit well together.
fact: In «A big chocolate bar before a match can give a quick lift then a slump and sit uneasily in the stomach», uneasily means the food is not settled in your stomach.
fact: Toast, a banana or cereal give steadier energy than a big chocolate bar.
exercise: In a story, «Tom looked around uneasily as the door creaked open.» What does uneasily show? | Boredom and sleepiness | Happiness and relaxation | *Worry or nervousness | Speed and excitement
exercise: «The happy ending and the sad news sit uneasily together.» What does sit uneasily mean here? | Fit perfectly | Are very loud | Sit very still | *Do not fit well together
exercise: Find and copy the word from «A big chocolate bar before a match can give a quick lift then a slump and sit uneasily in the stomach.» that tells how the chocolate sits. | *uneasily | match | steadier | toast
test: «She laughed uneasily when the teacher asked her name.» What does uneasily mean? | Sleepily and slowly | Loudly and happily | *Nervously and uncomfortably | Quickly and carelessly
test: Which food gives steadier energy, according to the sentence about the chocolate bar? | A quick lift | *Toast | A big chocolate bar | A slump
exam: Which sentence uses uneasily to mean not settled or not fitting well? | He ran fast to the bus stop | The sun was bright over the hills | *The two plans sit uneasily together | She read a book by the fire
